/*
 * BFS — CRC32 zero-byte advancement with immutable nibble transforms.
 *
 * The tables are immutable transforms for the reflected IEEE CRC-32
 * polynomial 0xEDB88320. Start with the one-zero-byte linear transform,
 * whose columns are the transforms of the 32 input basis bits. Repeatedly
 * square that GF(2) matrix to obtain transforms for 2^power zero bytes.
 * For each matrix, each table entry combines the four transformed basis bits
 * of one input nibble at bit offsets 0, 4, ..., 28. Applying one selected
 * length-power therefore takes eight nibble lookups and XORs. Constants are
 * generated at development time; there is no runtime initialization,
 * allocation, or I/O.
 *
 * CRC input/output follows bfs_crc32(): complement before and after the
 * linear operation. A zero length consequently returns initial unchanged.
 */
